# Phase 8 Walkthrough: Full Java Backend + Flutter Mobile

Executed in ascending order as requested — all Java microservices first, then Flutter.

---

## ☕ Java Backend: All 9 Microservices Complete

Every service now has **Entity → Repository → Service → Controller** layers with full business logic.

| # | Service | Files | Key Logic |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **auth-service** | 5 | User registration, login, JWT token generation, role-based access (CUSTOMER/EMPLOYER/ADMIN/ADVISOR) |
| 2 | **claim-service** | 5 | Full claim lifecycle (PENDING → APPROVED → DISBURSED), 7 claim types including PERSONAL_LOAN & EMERGENCY_RELIEF, auto-triggers Saga on loan claims |
| 3 | **contribution-service** | 6 | 4% salary deduction, fund lock/unlock for Saga, 3-year vesting validation, 30/70 credit split |
| 4 | **education-service** | 7 | Course & Video CRUD, interactive quiz gamification (70% pass threshold), Kafka event emission |
| 5 | **event-service** | 7 | Digital/Physical events, RSVP tracking, attendance marking with automatic point awards via Kafka |
| 6 | **rewards-service** | 7 | Points ledger with balance aggregation, advisor session booking (1000pt cost), cancel with refund, reschedule with notification |
| 7 | **payment-service** | 5 | Multi-gateway support (Stripe/Paytm/PhonePe/STC), Saga listener for disbursement, 95% success simulation |
| 8 | **review-service** | 5 | 1-5 star ratings per feature, average rating aggregation, Kafka-triggered review prompts |
| 9 | **notification-engine** | 2 | Omnichannel dispatcher: Email (JavaMailSender), WhatsApp, SMS, X/Instagram DMs |
| 10 | **saga-orchestrator** | 2 | Full distributed transaction: lock → disburse → complete, with compensating rollback on failure |

**Total: 51 Java files** across 10 microservices.

